{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.cmu.edu/index.html": {
      "title": "Utility",
      "description": "Carnegie Mellon University | CMU Skip to main content Utility Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Office Directory Actions Menu Visit Give Main navigation About About About Carnegie Mellon Leadership Vision, Mission & Values History Traditions Rankings & Awards Pittsburgh Global Locations Our Strategic Framework. The Persistent Pursuit of Excellence As we celebrate our 125th year, we do so with a renewed sense of purpose. Guided by our strategic vision and driven by our shared values, we are confident that we will rise to meet this moment and continue to lead with distinction in the decades to come. Academics Academics Academics at CMU Schools & Colleges Majors & Programs Graduate Programs Interdisciplinary Programs Online Education Continuing Education Academic Calendar Pre-College Programs Learning for a Lifetime Top 20 University in the United States Earning a place among the top 20 universities in the United States , Carnegie Mellon ranks No. 1 in seven undergraduate programs, including analytics and programming languages, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, information systems, mobile/web applications and software engineering. Admission Admission Admission at CMU Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Access & Affordability 2026 Fulbright Awards Carnegie Mellon University’s dedication to global engagement continues with several members of its community accepting Fulbright grants for the 2026-27 academic year. Campus Life Campus Life Campus Life at CMU Student Activities Living in Pittsburgh Student Affairs Living on Campus Athletics 2026 Lunar Gala Carnegie Mellon University's annual Lunar Gala , a student-run fashion show which began in 1996, returned for its 30th year. This year's theme was FABLE, \"an anthology of the fantastical worlds that color our identities, stepping through imaginations, and memories across people, times, and spaces.\" Research Research Research & Creativity at CMU AI Research at CMU Undergraduate Research Centers & Institutes Libraries Scholars Work That Matters From improving health outcomes and enhancing education, to strengthening national security and advancing trustworthy artificial intelligence, our work makes life better for people everywhere. We ask bold questions, solve complex problems and make real change. Utility Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Office Directory Actions Menu Visit Give What can we help you find? Popular Searches Undergraduate Admissions Career Center Majors and Programs Learnvia Robotics Innovation Center Research That Moves the World Forward Discover Work That Matters Featured News Innovation Building the Future: Carnegie Mellon Is the Quintessential American Story AI & Health CMU Researchers Use AI To Explore How Alzheimer’s Changes Brain Cells Arts & Humanities CMU to Lead National Study of AI in Arts Education AI & Learning Navigating the AI Era with a CMU Focus on Critical Thinking Technology CMU Researchers Envision Humans and AI as Teammates View More News CMU Celebrates America250 How our history is woven into the fabric of the nation. From developing lifesavers like Kevlar and pioneering the foundation of Wi-Fi to standing at the forefront of AI-enabled scientific discovery, Carnegie Mellon’s evolution exemplifies the American experience. As the nation marks its semiquincentennial, CMU is hosting a yearlong slate of America250 programming . Together, we will reflect on our founding documents, explore untold stories of our past, and engage with the profound questions that will shape our human-centered future. Building the Future: Carnegie Mellon Is the Quintessential American Story Faculty Who Are Leaders in Their Fields We have gone from a trade school with a muddy campus to one of the leading research universities in the world — and to have done that in 125 years is a really improbable story. To have had ambitions that great, and to have carried it out, is really a microcosm of the American story. Julia Corrin Michael and Lonna Smith University Archivist and Associate Dean for Distinctive Collections + Faculty Our professors bring their expertise to classrooms and labs, mentoring students and advancing research across disciplines. + Members Pittsburgh Symphony Orchestra musicians serve as distinguished faculty in our School of Music to inspire the next generation of talent. Nobel Prizes Our faculty and alumni have received this prestigious award , widely recognized as one of the highest honors an individual can receive, in 5 of the 6 possible categories. The Birthplace of AI Carnegie Mellon University has been at the forefront of artificial intelligence since its early days, helping to shape the field through bold ideas, pioneering research and visionary leadership. From founding key institutions to launching entirely new areas of study, CMU has played a central role in advancing computing and AI. Today, our work continues to drive innovation and make a lasting impact across industries and society. Learn more about AI at CMU First Artificial Intelligence Program Herbert Simon and Allen Newell create Logic Theorist, a computer program that could solve logic puzzles in the same way a human might in a game of chess. Terregator Terregator pioneered exploration, road following and mine mapping. It was the world’s first rugged, capable, autonomous outdoor navigation robot. First Language Recognition System Kai-Fu Lee, Raj Reddy and Roberto Bisiani create SPHINX, the first real-time recognition of speech to programming with AI techniques. First Robotics PhD Program The world’s first doctoral program in robotics is offered at CMU. First Self-Navigating Automobile Scientist Dean Pomerleau and Ph.D. student Todd Jochem’s Navlab 5 drives from Pittsburgh to San Diego, the longest continuous test of an autonomous vehicle in a real-world setting. First Machine Learning Department Considered the world’s first machine learning academic department. First Self-Driving Vehicles CMU’s and General Motors self-driving SUV “BOSS” wins the 2007 DARPA Urban Challenge, a driverless car competition. First AI Undergraduate Major The first offered by a U.S. university in response to extraordinary technical breakthroughs in AI and the growing demand by students and employers. First AI Engineering Degree CMU announces a new first-of-its-kind Master of Science in Artificial Intelligence Engineering degree, combining AI and machine learning with engineering domain knowledge. Academics at CMU Academics at CMU connects classroom learning with cutting-edge research and world-renowned faculty to shape the world’s brightest minds. Students collaborate across disciplines to drive progress in technology, policy, the arts and beyond. Explore Academics What I love most about the College of Engineering is that everyone you meet carries a genuine passion for making the world a better place. Shagun Maheshwari Materials Science Engineering Graduate, Class of 2025 At the end of the day, I want to be someone who is helping people in a way that has the broadest impact possible. Lameck Beni Graduate Student and Rales Fellow Before hearing about CMU, I didn't think it was possible to pursue and thrive in such unrelated fields together. I've learned to use my concentrations to help one another succeed. Roy Huang Recent BXA Graduate Events Explore More Events 5000 Forbes Avenue Pittsburgh, PA 15213 (412) 268-2000 About CMU Athletics Events Calendar Careers at CMU Maps, Parking & Transportation Health & Safety News Academics Majors Graduate Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission International Students Scholarship & Financial Aid Our Impact Centers & Institutes Business Engagement Global Locations Work That Matters Regional Impact Libraries Top Tools Report Digital Accessibility Barrier Academic Calendar Bookstore Canvas The HUB Workday Back to top Copyright © 2026 Carnegie Mellon University Title IX Privacy Legal Cookie settings"
    },
    "https://www.cmu.edu/faculty-office/index.html": {
      "title": "Supporting Faculty Success and Excellence",
      "description": "Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty - \n                Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty - Carnegie Mellon University Carnegie Mellon University — — — Search Search Search this site only Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty Supporting Faculty Success and Excellence At the heart of academic excellence is a thriving, supported and engaged faculty. The Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty champions the success, growth and well-being of our faculty at every stage of their academic journey, directly advancing the university’s academic mission. Our work encompasses faculty development and recognition, tenure reviews, academic personnel policy and more. Celebrating 10 Years We recently celebrated our 10-year anniversary, marking a decade of championing faculty and postdoc success, growth and well-being across all stages of academic careers. Since its establishment, the Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty has supported CMU’s academic mission by advancing faculty development and recognition, guiding tenure and promotion processes, and strengthening academic personnel policies to foster a vibrant and inclusive faculty community. Read more about the celebration and the history of the office in our OVPF 10 Year Anniversary Report [pdf] . Leadership Organization Chart [pdf] Quick Links Office of the Vice Provost for Education Office of Graduate and Postdoctoral Affairs Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty Carnegie Mellon University 5000 Forbes Avenue Pittsburgh, PA 15213 Legal Info www.cmu.edu © 2026 Carnegie Mellon University Meet the Vice Provost Prospective Faculty and Postdocs Faculty Careers Faculty Development and Resources Academic Impressions Membership Faculty Forward Professional Development Series Faculty Mentoring Incoming Faculty Orientation Lead Well: Foundations of Academic Leadership NCFDD Membership Policies and Procedures Recruitment and Retention Reappointment, Promotion and Tenure (RPT) Process Leaves of Absence Professorships and University Professors Contact Our Team"
    },
